  abstract={Summary <p>The accelerated pace of the implementation of AI in architecture has given rise to a fascinating field of inquiry, demanding rigorous examination and investigation. One of the most significant advantages of incorporating AI into architecture is the ability to expand the human mind's creative capabilities. AI tools and algorithms offer architects access to a vast repository of data, design precedents and advanced computational capabilities, enabling them to generate innovative ideas and solutions. By considering the values and narratives embedded within architecture's cultural and historical contexts, designers can craft more inclusive, meaningful and people&#x2010;centred designs that resonate with the diverse communities they serve. To that end, machine learning, deep learning and other concepts that are subsumed under the umbrella term &#x2018;artificial intelligence&#x2019; can help designers explore the large data vaults of culture in order to inform, expand and enrich the design space of architecture.</p>},
