  abstract={Generative AI (Gen AI), a rapidly evolving technology, has gained substantial attention for its capacity to simulate human-like responses and engage in natural language interactions. While prior research has investigated the general landscape of Gen AI tools, the current study focuses specifically on exploring how learners utilized ChatGPT to personalize their learning experiences. Drawing on qualitative research method, data were collected through open-ended survey from learners utilizing ChatGPT in their educational activities. The study utilized ATLAS.ti to conduct an inductive analysis, identifying recurring themes within the data. The findings revealed that learners utilized ChatGPT to personalize their learning experiences in areas such as language learning, writing enhancement, reading comprehension, research support, adaptive feedback, and access to information resources. The study emphasizes the importance of a balanced approach to ChatGPT usage in education, underscoring its implications for learners. It also calls for further research in the area of personalized learning.},
