  number={},
  pages={234-238},
  abstract={This study explores the integration of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) and mind maps in high school English reading instruction. Based on constructivist theory, a three-dimensional teaching framework of "data-driven previewing - collaborative construction and deepening -intelligent feedback and improvement" is constructed. A specific teaching case, "Living Legends," is designed to enhance students’ reading comprehension and logical thinking. The framework leverages GenAI for precise resource recommendation, intelligent evaluation, and mind maps for visualizing thinking processes. This integration helps effectively improve reading efficiency and cultivate higher-order thinking skills. Despite limitations like technological constraints and potential over-reliance on tools, this study provides valuable insights into the innovative application of GenAI and mind maps in language teaching.},
