  booktitle={2025 6th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Electromechanical Automation (AIEA)}, 
  title={Knowledge Graph Analysis of Fault Diagnosis of Rotating Machinery Based on Artificial Intelligence}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={160-167},
  abstract={Based on bibliometrics and knowledge graph methods, this article systematically reviews the evolution path and research trends of artificial intelligence (AI) in the field of rotating machinery fault diagnosis. Using the Web of Science (WoS) core collection of literature as the data source, combined with CiteSpace tool for keyword co-occurrence, emergent word detection, and collaborative network analysis, this study reveals the technical context of the field's transition from traditional signal processing to deep learning paradigm. It is found that multimodal data fusion, migration learning and anti noise models are the current research hotspots, while small sample learning, edge computing adaptation and interpretable AI are bottlenecks that need to be broken through. This study provides a dynamic knowledge graph for academia and a theoretical basis for optimizing intelligent diagnostic systems in industry through quantitative and visual analysis, promoting the development of fault diagnosis technology towards high reliability and strong generalization.},
