  booktitle={2024 2nd International Conference on Disruptive Technologies (ICDT)}, 
  title={Generative AI in FinTech: Generating Images Based on Predefined Lists of Stock Keeping Units Using Product Descriptions}, 
  year={2024},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={549-554},
  abstract={Generative AI in FinTech is a new technology that uses AI to generate images based on predefined lists of Stock Keeping Units (SKUs) using product descriptions provided by users. It leverages an AI-based tool to produce custom product images to accurately sync with individual SKUs. This technology allows FinTech companies to create product images to help promote their ecommerce sites or offline stores, while still adhering to product description specifics that define user intent. With more accurate product images, customers are able to more easily find the product they are looking for. Generative AI in FinTech also helps to reduce the manual effort it takes for businesses to define and recreate product images for customers, saving cost and time. Overall, this technology is a key breakthrough in FinTech's efforts to create seamless customer experiences.},
